## 3. URL / Link Analysis

**Tool used:** URLScan.io + CyberChef (to decode the base64 HTML body first)

| # | Displayed link text | Actual destination URL | URLScan verdict | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | "Clique aqui" (view images) | https://blog1seguimentmydomaine2bra.me/ | No classification (see notes) | Same URL reused for main CTA |
| 2 | "Resgatar Agora" (Redeem Now — main CTA) | https://blog1seguimentmydomaine2bra.me/ | No classification (see notes) | |

- **Domain age / registrar:** TLS cert for the domain was issued ~Sept 14, 2023 — 5 days before this email was sent, consistent with a domain freshly stood up for this campaign.
- **Redirect chain observed:** Scans close to the campaign date (Sept 24, 2023) show 20 HTTP transactions across 9 domains/IPs before landing on `/lander`.
- **Behavior notes:** A scan close to the campaign window returned a fake "verifying connection" loading page instead of a real form — consistent with cloaking against scanner/bot traffic (real victims would see a fake Bradesco/Livelo login form; automated tools get shown a decoy). Later scans (mid-2024) show the domain briefly unresolvable, then eventually resolving to unrelated generic parked content (hotel/retail ads) — consistent with the domain expiring and being picked up by a parking service after the campaign ended.
- Does the link destination match the displayed text or claimed brand? **No** — nothing in the domain relates to Bradesco or Livelo.

