## 6. Red Flags Summary

1. From-address domain (atendimento.com.br) has zero relation to the impersonated brand (Bradesco/Livelo)
2. SPF/DKIM/DMARC all fail or error — no valid authentication for a message claiming to be from a major bank
3. Sending infrastructure is a generic VPS (DigitalOcean IP range), not bank mail infrastructure
4. Destination URL is an unrelated, freshly-registered throwaway domain with no brand connection
5. Urgency + reward bait ("points expiring today," ~93,000 points) designed to drive an immediate click
6. Landing site shows scanner-cloaking behavior, typical of credential-harvesting kits evading detection

---

## 7. Verdict

**Classification:** Phishing
**Confidence:** High
**Recommended action:** Block sender domain and originating IP at the mail gateway; add destination domain to blocklist; report to email provider; no user action needed to remediate (sample sourced from a research honeypot, not a live inbox).

**Analyst summary:** This message impersonates Bradesco/Livelo to pressure recipients into clicking a "redeem points" link before they "expire." All three email authentication checks (SPF/DKIM/DMARC) fail or error, the sending and landing infrastructure have no legitimate connection to the claimed brand, and the landing domain shows scanner-cloaking behavior consistent with a credential-harvesting phishing kit.
